<h2>Add activity</h2>
@*
    POST form: asp-action="Add" -> action="/Activity/Add", PLUS a hidden __RequestVerificationToken
    (anti-forgery token) that [ValidateAntiForgeryToken] on the Add action checks.
*@
<form asp-action="Add" method="post">
    <input name="text" placeholder="What happened?" />
    <button type="submit">Add</button>
</form>

<h2>Look up a day</h2>
@*
    GET form: asp-action="Day" -> action="/Activity/Day". No token is added for GET (GET must never change data).
    The browser puts the inputs in the URL: /Activity/Day?day=2026-11-05, which our custom binder reads.
*@
<form asp-action="Day" method="get">
    <input name="day" placeholder="yyyy-MM-dd" />
    <button type="submit">Show</button>
</form>
<p>Try a bad value like <a href="/Activity/Day?day=05/11/2026">05/11/2026</a> to see the binder reject it.</p>
